          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फलना — phalnā — \"to bear fruit; to pay off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आँगन का पेड़ बहुत फला। Āṁgan kā peṛ bahut phalā. The tree in the courtyard bore a lot of fruit."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): वह पेड़ फला, vah peṛ phalā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फलना (phalnā) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit phalati, \"bears fruit\" (CDIAL 9057)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
